# netsurf: descriptors as WebIDL and ECMAScript define them -- what
# hCaptcha's collector reads (patch 280)
# Generated 2026-10-13
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 279)
#
# hsw's main collector call, compared with Chromium's after 273-279
# (docs/wasm-hcaptcha-measurement.md), still read different descriptors:
#
#  A. WebIDL operations and attributes on the interface prototypes are
#     enumerable and an operation is named for its property; 346 of 998
#     here were not enumerable (getContext, toDataURL, measureText,
#     Permissions.query, ...), 12 misnamed (Node.prototype.appendChild
#     anonymous, URL.prototype.toString, ...).
#  B. Intl objects: [object Intl.DateTimeFormat] ... (they said
#     [object Object]); their methods named and not enumerable, as
#     ECMAScript built-ins are (resolvedOptions was anonymous, enumerable).
#  C. window's attributes are accessors -- navigator, screen, crypto,
#     localStorage, document, top, ... ([Replaceable] ones -- self, frames,
#     screen, innerWidth, devicePixelRatio, performance, ... -- take a value
#     set on them; name and opener keep one); here data properties, the
#     viewport ones not enumerable. console, CSS, NodeFilter stop
#     enumerating.
#  D. document.location enumerates (it stays configurable: the bridge
#     redefines it).
#  E. contentWindow / contentDocument are HTMLIFrameElement.prototype's,
#     not every element's; and an iframe / img wrapper gets its interface's
#     prototype (macsurf_qjs.c qjs_dom_ctor_proto built "HTMLIframeElement",
#     "HTMLImgElement": both were [object HTMLElement], instanceof only by a
#     hasInstance stand-in; the table now covers iframe, img, h1-h6, br, hr,
#     li, fieldset, optgroup, datalist, q / blockquote, ins / del, colgroup,
#     thead / tbody / tfoot).
#  F. getComputedStyle's result and element.style are CSSStyleDeclarations
#     (prototype CSSStyleDeclaration.prototype, which holds nothing they
#     could inherit by mistake); the computed style's __inline goes to the
#     private record.
#  G. localStorage / sessionStorage are Storages ([object Storage]).
#  Also: the polyfill's six __vita marks on functions go to the private
#  record, as the __vb ones did in 276.
#
# The demo still refuses the engine (797 bytes).
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/JS-descriptors.html (DESCRIPTORS 7/7, Chromium 7/7;
# the build before fails 1-6).
